{
  "_comment": [
    "Value slug -> HadeethEnc category ids (hadeethenc.com/api/v1), from docs/hackathon/research/r1-hadeethenc-quranenc-mcp.md Appendix B.",
    "categories: every hadith in the category (the list endpoint includes sub-categories) is a candidate (relevance: category).",
    "keyword_only_categories: a hadith only counts if its Arabic title/matn contains one of the value's keywords_ar (relevance: ar_keyword), or its English title/text contains a word starting with one of keywords_en (relevance: en_keyword). Arabic is compared after normalisation (no tashkeel, alef/ya/ta-marbuta folded), so records without English still match.",
    "keywords_ar (optional): specific Arabic keywords for the value. Without it the child-voice keywords_ar in content/values.json are used (weaker). Used only to rank and to gate keyword_only_categories.",
    "Some values have no HadeethEnc category of their own (justice, caring for orphans, not wasting): they are found by keyword inside the broad categories that hold the good hadith (for example Bukhari 6005 sits in 511, Muslim 1827 in 282).",
    "deny_list: r1 section 2.6. A hadith in ANY of these categories (or a sub-category, or listed under them) is never a candidate; it needs a human age check. 324 (Paradise and Hell descriptions) was unblocked by the lead (hope first): its hadith are candidates and draft_from_page.py age-screens graphic ones to 10-13.",
    "Ids come from a 26 Sep 2026 third-party snapshot and a Postman sample; confirm the titles after the first pull (categories.en.json in the cache)."
  ],
